# Phase charter — Dandan format (issue #5169), run dandan-5169

Source: `.planning/dandan-5169/brief/issue-5169.md`, pinned `d95cc66019`. Run base (`BASE_SHA`) = HEAD `7238b9c183`. `git diff --stat d95cc66019 HEAD` touches only `casting.rs`/`casting_costs.rs`/`oracle_casting.rs`/`oracle_cost.rs`/skill docs — none of the brief's anchor files — so the brief's code-shape claims carry to `BASE_SHA` unchanged; each phase still buys its own claims per the charter contract below.

**Deliverable:** one PR to `phase-rs/phase` main closing #5169, all 11 phases below as sequential checkpoint commits. Total estimate ~9,600 LOC added (range 6,800–13,300; basis and per-phase figures in the planner report), well under the ~30,000-line single-PR ceiling — no split by size is warranted.

**Format group:** `Multiplayer`, registry position after Momir, before Custom. **Skills used across phases:** `add-engine-effect`, `add-static-ability`, `add-engine-variant` (gate, Phase 1 and Phase 2), `add-interactive-effect` (Phase 8), `oracle-parser`, `card-test`.

## Phase list

1. S1 — Format registration, axes, protocol, AI force-keep re-gate
2. PREREQ-0 + CR 612 text-changing primitive (Magical Hack, Crystal Spray)
3. S2a — Canonical-seat storage authority
4. S2b-1 — Read sweep: core game/effects files
5. S2b-2 — Read sweep: analysis/ai_support/types + cross-crate (phase-ai, engine-wasm, phase-llm)
6. S2c — Filter owner-axis collapse + count dedup
7. S3 — Hand-entry ownership rebind
8. S4 — Mulligan declare round, FreeReveal, pregame dealer
9. S4b + PREREQ-3 + S6 — In-game simultaneous-draw dealer, Day's Undoing wheel split, deck-out verification
10. S7 — Frontend shared-pile display
11. S8 — AI consumer rerouting

Each phase's recursive T1∧T2 check is stated inline; none trips the conjunction (shown per phase).

---

### Phase 1 — S1: Format registration, axes, protocol, AI force-keep re-gate

**Goal.** Register `GameFormat::Dandan` as a complete axis-driven format: constructor, the 18 compiler-forced exhaustive arms, the 5 new typed predicate axis methods (shared zones, deal order, free-reveal mulligan, hand-entry rebind, opening-hands-equivalent), registry entry, protocol/lobby-version bump with a frozen `MIN_LOBBY_PROTOCOL_FOR_DANDAN` floor, and the AI force-keep re-gate so a Dandan hand is evaluated on its own axis rather than inheriting Momir's `supplies_fixed_deck` ForceKeep. No shared-zone runtime behavior lands here — the axis methods return typed values consumers read in later phases.

**Scope rule.** `crates/engine/src/types/format.rs`; `crates/engine/src/game/deck_validation.rs` (`quick_dandan_check`, `evaluate_dandan`, mirroring `quick_momir_check`/`evaluate_momir`); `crates/engine/src/types/custom_format.rs` (`CommanderEligibilityRule::from_source_format`); `crates/engine-wasm/src/lib.rs` (`is_card_commander_eligible_for_format` arm only — the boot-guard edit in the same file belongs to Phase 3); `crates/engine/tests/integration/custom_format_schema.rs`; `client/src/types.ts`, `client/src/data/formatRegistry.ts`, `client/src/adapter/ws-adapter.ts` (`lobbyProtocolRequiredForFormat` + new `MIN_LOBBY_PROTOCOL_FOR_DANDAN`, precedent `MIN_LOBBY_PROTOCOL_FOR_FREEFORM_FORMATS`), `client/src/network/protocol.ts` (`WIRE_PROTOCOL_VERSION`); whichever test file holds `FORMAT_SHAPES` for `deckUrlImport` (grep `FORMAT_SHAPES` at scope-freeze); `crates/lobby-broker/src/protocol.rs` (`PROTOCOL_VERSION`); `scripts/check-protocol-version.mjs`; `crates/phase-ai/src/policies/mulligan/fixed_deck_keepables.rs`.

**Claims to establish.**
- `GameFormat::FreeformCommander` precedes `Custom(CustomFormatId)` in declaration order and `GameFormat::iter()` walks that order — buy by `grep -n "FreeformCommander\|Custom(CustomFormatId)" crates/engine/src/types/format.rs` (measured at Phase-charter time: lines 145/152, confirmed present in that order at `BASE_SHA`; re-confirm unchanged at phase start).
- `FixedDeckKeepMulligan::score` gates `ForceKeep` on `state.format_config.supplies_fixed_deck` alone, with no format-identity check — buy by reading `crates/phase-ai/src/policies/mulligan/fixed_deck_keepables.rs` at phase start; a Dandan-config unit test asserting non-ForceKeep is the closing measurement, not a prior grep.
- The 18 exhaustive-arm sites are compiler-forced, not enumerable in advance beyond the brief's list — buy by adding the variant and reading the compiler's own missing-arm errors; do not hand-verify the count.

**Verification plan.** Unit tests: `FromStr`/`Display` round-trip, `FormatConfig::dandan()` field values (20 life, 2 players, `DeckSizeRule::Exactly(80)`, `supplies_fixed_deck: true`, `command_zone: false`), `has_unrepresentable_auxiliary_deck_component() == true` (revert-failing: flip to `false` and show `CustomFormatDef::from_lobby_config` would accept a Dandan lobby as Custom), each new axis method's Dandan-vs-other-format arms, `MIN_LOBBY_PROTOCOL_FOR_DANDAN` wired into `lobbyProtocolRequiredForFormat`, `FixedDeckKeepMulligan` non-ForceKeep on Dandan config with a sibling assertion that Momir is still ForceKeep (paired positive/negative). A full booted-Dandan-game test is `DEFERRED(phase 3)` — deck loading doesn't exist yet.

**Deferral list.** Shared-zone runtime resolution (→ Phase 3–6), ownership rebind (→ Phase 7), mulligan declare round consuming the free-reveal axis (→ Phase 8), pile-holder exposure to frontend (→ Phase 10), AI accessor rerouting beyond force-keep (→ Phase 11).

**Seam notes.** `crates/engine-wasm/src/lib.rs` is also touched by Phase 3 (boot guard) at a different function — sequential, no overlap risk.

**T1∧T2 check.** 1 unit (one `add-engine-variant` pass). T1 fails (needs ≥2) regardless of T2 — conjunction cannot fire.

