### Phase 2 — PREREQ-0 + CR 612 text-changing primitive (Magical Hack, Crystal Spray)

**Goal.** Two independent, unrelated-to-shared-zones fixes bundled for phase-count economy: (a) accept `Effect::Counter { countered_spell_zone: Some(_), .. }` as a replacement carrier in the swallow check, fixing Memory Lapse's false-positive `unsupported` status; (b) build the general CR 612 word-substitution primitive — a `Layer::Text` `ContinuousModification` over a typed word domain (`BasicLandType`, `ColorWord`) — and cover both known instances of the class: Magical Hack (domain `{BasicLandType}`, indefinite duration) and Crystal Spray (domain `{ColorWord, BasicLandType}`, player chooses which, until-end-of-turn duration). This is "build for the class" applied at the phase boundary: one primitive, two cards, one phase, so no half-built primitive persists across a phase boundary.

**Scope rule.** `crates/engine/src/parser/swallow_check.rs` (PREREQ-0); `crates/engine/src/types/ability.rs` (new `Layer::Text` variant, beside `SetTextName`/`SetChosenName`); the CR 612 parser addition (file TBD by planner — trace `Cleave` in `crates/engine/src/database/synthesis.rs` and `Overload` in `crates/engine/src/game/effects/overload.rs` first, per the brief, to find the right parser/resolver seam; neither traced file is itself edited unless the trace shows a genuine shared seam); the resolver/effect-handler file the parser dispatches to.

**Claims to establish.**
- `effect_is_replacement_carrier` in `swallow_check.rs` does not currently accept `Effect::Counter { countered_spell_zone: Some(_), .. }` — buy by grepping the function body at phase start; the coverage regeneration command in the brief is the closing measurement (Memory Lapse flips to `supported:true`... or the applicable non-`Unimplemented` status).
- No CR 612 text-substitution primitive exists in the engine today — buy by grepping `data/engine-inventory.json` (regenerate via `cargo engine-inventory` first) for `SetTextName`/`SetChosenName` siblings; absence of a substitution variant is the claim.

**Verification plan.** PREREQ-0: one unit test per the brief's own sizing ("about 5 lines... one test"), revert-failing (remove the accepted arm, Memory Lapse reports `unsupported` again). CR 612 primitive: cast-pipeline tests (per `/card-test`) for both Magical Hack (permanent domain, indefinite duration, e.g. "swampwalk"→"islandwalk"-style land-type substitution on a target permanent) and Crystal Spray (until-end-of-turn duration, player choice of domain), plus a hostile fixture — a word that is NOT a land-type/color word in context (CR 612.2's "used in the correct way" carve-out) must not be substituted. Not deferred — fully independent of shared-zone work.

**Deferral list.** None — this phase closes both PREREQ-0 and the full CR 612 primitive (both known instances) in one pass.

**Seam notes.** None with other phases; this primitive's files are untouched by any other phase in this run.

**T1∧T2 check.** 2 units (PREREQ-0's swallow-check fix; the CR 612 primitive covering both cards is one unit per the class-pass anchor). Estimated scope paths: swallow_check.rs, its test, ability.rs, the parser file, the resolver file, 2 card-level test files ≈ 7. T1 fires, T2 (7 < 13) does not — conjunction cannot fire.

