### Phase 3 — S2a: Canonical-seat storage authority

**Goal.** Introduce the canonical-seat concept (lowest `PlayerId`, fixed at setup, never recomputed) and route every *write* to library/graveyard storage through it, so journal replay stays deterministic. Covers: `GameState::library_of`/`graveyard_of` (and `_mut`) accessors; write-side canonicalization in `zones.rs` (`remove_from_zone`, `add_to_zone`, `move_to_library_at_index`, `reorder_within_library`, `zone_container_len`), `game/library.rs` (`resolve_and_apply_library_shuffle`/`apply_resolved_library_shuffle`, storage resolves to canonical seat while `ResolvedLibraryShuffleCommand.player` stays the acting player), the raw writers in `engine_resolution_choices.rs` and `effects/conjure.rs`; deck provisioning (`dandan_fixed_deck_names` beside `momir_fixed_deck_names`, a Dandan branch in `load_and_hydrate_decks` loading one 80-card pile into the canonical seat only); the `engine-wasm` empty-library boot guard routed through the accessor; `select_cards_to_draw` in `effects/draw.rs` routed through the accessor (covers the draw-selection and empty-library-flag path for single draws); `mulligan.rs::shuffle_hand_into_library` routed through the library accessor or `resolve_and_apply_library_shuffle`; library-knowledge epoch keys (`advance_library_knowledge_epoch`, `library_knowledge_epoch`, `library_knowledge_boundary_generation`, `LibraryKnowledgeStamp.library_owner`, `viewer_knows_card_identity`, `canonicalize_library_knowledge_epoch`) resolved to the canonical seat.

**Scope rule.** `crates/engine/src/types/game_state.rs` (new accessor methods); `crates/engine/src/game/zones.rs`; `crates/engine/src/game/library.rs`; `crates/engine/src/game/engine_resolution_choices.rs`; `crates/engine/src/game/effects/conjure.rs`; `crates/engine/src/game/deck_loading.rs`; `crates/engine-wasm/src/lib.rs` (boot-guard function only); `crates/engine/src/game/effects/draw.rs` (`select_cards_to_draw`); `crates/engine/src/game/mulligan.rs` (`shuffle_hand_into_library`, `draw_n` — the brief notes `draw_n` reads `player.library[0]` directly and is routed separately from `shuffle_hand_into_library`); the file(s) implementing the library-knowledge epoch functions (locate at phase start — the brief names the functions, not the file, and this file was not touched in the pin→HEAD diff so its location is stable but unconfirmed by this charter).

**Claims to establish.**
- `GameState` has no shared-pile concept today: `Player.library`/`Player.graveyard` are read per-seat everywhere with no canonical-seat resolution — buy by grepping `zones.rs`/`game_state.rs` for any existing "canonical"/"shared" seat concept at phase start; absence is the claim.
- `zone_authority_census.py --list` enumerates today's zone-write population as a regenerable command (confirmed reproducible: 48 classified production hits in 29 rows at `BASE_SHA`) — re-run at phase start, not cited as a frozen count.
- `mulligan.rs::shuffle_hand_into_library` today raw-shuffles the mulliganing seat's own `library` field, which for the non-canonical seat is the empty seat, leaving the shared pile's actual order unchanged (CR 103.5 violation) — buy by reading the function body at phase start.

**Verification plan.** Deck-load test: Dandan boots with one 80-card pile on the canonical seat, empty on the other, both seats' `library_of()` reads return the same pile. Draw test: the non-canonical seat's `select_cards_to_draw` reads from the shared pile via the accessor (revert-failing: bypass the accessor and show the non-canonical seat draws nothing). Shuffle test: the shared pile's order changes when the non-canonical seat mulligans, and separately when it FreeReveals (per the brief) — the FreeReveal leg is `DEFERRED(phase 8)` since `FreeReveal` doesn't exist as a choice until Phase 8; the mulligan-shuffle leg is testable now via the existing `Mulligan` choice. Library-knowledge test: mixed-owner cards in the one shared library keep correct per-viewer knowledge after the epoch-key fix (revert-failing: un-resolve the key to owner-only and show stale knowledge for the non-canonical seat). Card-level "Brainstorm works from either seat" is `DEFERRED(phase 4 or 5)` — the effect's own read site isn't swept until S2b.

**Deferral list.** Read-sweep of the ~150+16 remaining single-player read sites (→ Phases 4–5), filter owner/controller-axis collapse and count dedup (→ Phase 6), hand-entry ownership rebind (→ Phase 7), FreeReveal's shuffle leg (→ Phase 8).

**Seam notes.** `crates/engine-wasm/src/lib.rs` also touched by Phase 1 (different function, sequential). `crates/engine/src/game/mulligan.rs` also touched by Phase 8 (declare round, built on top of this phase's now-correct shuffle routing). `crates/engine/src/game/effects/draw.rs` also touched by Phase 9 (multi-player dealer frame wraps this phase's single-draw routing).

**T1∧T2 check.** 1 unit (one canonical-storage-authority mechanic, many lockstep files). T1 fails regardless of T2 — conjunction cannot fire.

