### Phase 4 — S2b-1: Read sweep, core game/effects files

**Goal.** Convert single-player `.library`/`.graveyard` reads to the Phase 3 accessor across the engine's core game-logic and effect-handler files. All-players flat-map sites (`targeting.rs::zone_object_ids`, `costs.rs`, `triggers.rs`, `visibility.rs`, `quantity.rs::object_count_matching_candidate_ids`) stay raw by design — confirmed by their own module: they already return the pile once under canonical storage, so routing them per-seat would duplicate it N times. Fold the private (player, zone) resolvers `choose_from_zone.rs::object_ids_in_player_zone` and `restrictions.rs::player_zone_ids` into the accessor.

**Scope rule.** `crates/engine/src/game/` (files with unswept `.library`/`.graveyard` reads per the regenerating command, excluding files already fully covered by Phase 3's write-side edits: `zones.rs`, `library.rs`, `engine_resolution_choices.rs`, `conjure.rs`, `deck_loading.rs`, `draw.rs`, `mulligan.rs`); `crates/engine/src/game/effects/` (all files with occurrences: `reveal_top.rs`, `exile_top.rs`, `search_library.rs`, `cascade.rs`, `choose_card.rs`, `choose_from_zone.rs`, `collect_evidence.rs`, `dig.rs`, `explore.rs`, `manifest_dread.rs`, `mill.rs`, `ripple.rs`, `scry.rs`, `seek.rs`, `separate_piles.rs`, `surveil.rs`, `bounce.rs`, `clash.rs`, `discover.rs`, `exile_face_down_pile.rs`, `exile_from_top_until.rs`, `forage.rs`, `free_cast_from_zones.rs`, `heist.rs`, `put_on_top.rs`, `rad_counters.rs`, `reveal_until.rs`, `stack_reach.rs`); `casting.rs`, `casting_costs.rs`, `cost_payability.rs`, `costs.rs` (verify-only: confirm it belongs in the "stays raw" class, no edit), `engine.rs`, `engine_payment_choices.rs`, `replacement.rs`, `visibility.rs` (verify-only), `augment.rs`, `derived.rs`, `derived_views.rs`, `morph.rs`, `restrictions.rs`, `layers.rs`, `engine_debug.rs`. Regenerating command: `python3 <brief-dir>/scripts/count_reads.py HEAD '\.(library|graveyard)\b(?!\s*\()' -v` re-run at scope-freeze to materialize the exact file list against this directory scope.

**Claims to establish.** Each swept file's occurrence is a single-player read (not an all-players flat-map) — buy per-file at phase-plan time by reading the call site; the brief's classification (targeting/costs/triggers/visibility stay raw) is the starting claim, re-confirmed by grep since neither file changed pin→HEAD.

**Verification plan.** Card-level cast-pipeline tests (per `/card-test`) for the cards whose relevant effect lives in a swept file and is reachable now: Brainstorm, Mental Note, Predict, Telling Time (Dig→Hand), Halimar Depths (`reveal_top`/similar). Each test drives the effect from the non-canonical seat and asserts it reads/writes the shared pile, revert-failing by reverting that file's accessor swap alone. Accumulated Knowledge's full behavior (dedup) is `DEFERRED(phase 6)`; its plain per-copy draw is testable here.

**Deferral list.** `quantity.rs`'s `CardTypeSetSource` dedup arm and `QuantityRef::ZoneCardCount`/`GraveyardSize` (→ Phase 6, same file — Phase 5 or this phase converts `quantity.rs`'s individual reads first, whichever phase's scope-freeze claims it); filter owner/controller collapse (→ Phase 6); cross-crate reads (→ Phase 5).

**Seam notes.** None of this phase's files are touched by any other phase except where noted (quantity.rs, handled in the T1∧T2 check below).

**T1∧T2 check.** 1 unit (the read-sweep mechanic, uniformly applied). T1 fails regardless of T2 — conjunction cannot fire.

