### Phase 7 — S3: Hand-entry ownership rebind

**Goal.** Under the format's hand-entry-rebind axis (from Phase 1), a zone move from a shared zone into a hand carries the receiving player, and `obj.owner := receiver` before containers are chosen, at the Hand-destination seam in `zone_pipeline.rs` (not in each resolver). The receiver is the drawer for draws and the opening deal, and the effect's "your hand" player for Dig→Hand (Telling Time) and ChangeZone Graveyard→Hand (Haunted Fengraf). With the rebind in place, every cast (`casting_costs::finalize_cast_with_phyrexian_choices_inner` → `ZoneMoveRequest::casting_to_stack`) and every land play (`engine.rs::handle_play_land`) is by the owner by construction — no cast- or land-play-time stamp is added, since no Dandan card casts or plays from the shared library/graveyard directly. The rebind must replay: `apply_resolved_zone_change` refuses with `OwnerMismatch` when `object.owner != command.owner` (confirmed present at `zones.rs`), so the rebind is carried by the zone-change command or journaled as its own typed command (the `ResolvedControllerOverrideCommand` precedent in `resolved_commands.rs` shows the shape); the phase plan picks one based on whether journal replay is live for the chosen approach.

**Scope rule.** `crates/engine/src/game/zone_pipeline.rs` (the Hand-destination seam); `crates/engine/src/types/resolved_commands.rs` (only if the journaled-command approach is chosen); `crates/engine/src/game/zones.rs` (only if `apply_resolved_zone_change`'s `OwnerMismatch` check itself needs to accept the rebound owner — compiler-forced or test-forced, not a design choice made here).

**Claims to establish.** `apply_resolved_zone_change` refuses `OwnerMismatch` on `object.owner != command.owner` today (confirmed at `zones.rs:943,1078` at `BASE_SHA`) — re-confirm at phase start; this is why a raw field write on `obj.owner` is insufficient and the rebind must go through a command path.

**Verification plan.** Fixture (from the brief, fully specified): the non-canonical seat draws (and separately Telling-Times) a creature from the shared library and gets it with owner = itself; it casts the creature; the other seat Control-Magics it (controller changes, owner unchanged); Unsubstantiate returns it to the caster's (owner's) hand. Revert leg: remove the rebind, the card lands in the canonical seat's hand at draw instead (paired positive/negative, both legs in the brief already).

**Deferral list.** None — S3 is fully self-contained given Phase 3's accessor.

**Seam notes.** None — `zone_pipeline.rs` is not touched by any other phase in this run.

**T1∧T2 check.** 1 unit. T1 fails regardless of T2 — conjunction cannot fire.

---

### Phase 8 — S4: Mulligan declare round, FreeReveal, pregame dealer

**Goal.** Add a CR 103.5 declare round for formats with a shared library (gated on the shared-zone axis): Mulligan and FreeReveal declarations are recorded without redrawing; once every `Declare` entry has declared, all redrawers are dealt interleaved, active player first, through one pregame interleave primitive (`apnap_order_from`) shared by the opening deal (`start_mulligan`) and the round's redraws. Add `MulliganChoice::FreeReveal` (modeled on `UseSerumPowder`'s shape: validated at declare time, gated on the `Declare` phase, legal only when `mulligan_count == 0` and the settled-decision-1 hand predicate holds — fewer than two lands OR fewer than two nonland cards); it reveals the hand, returns it through `shuffle_hand_into_library`, and redraws through the dealer, incrementing nothing and bottoming nothing. Extend consumers: `game/interaction.rs`'s `GameAction::MulliganDecision` match, `ai_support/candidates.rs` (emit FreeReveal), phase-ai `search.rs`'s `deterministic_choice` and `fallback_action`, client `types.ts` `MulliganChoice` + GamePage mulligan buttons + the `en` locale's `gamePage.mulligan` keys (mirrors follow, no separate edit). `manabrew-compat` gets no protocol output for FreeReveal — Dandan is declared unsupported on that adapter.

**Scope rule.** `crates/engine/src/types/actions.rs` (`MulliganChoice`); `crates/engine/src/game/mulligan.rs` (`MulliganDecisionEntry`/`MulliganDecisionPhase`, `advance_after_decision`, the declare-round machinery, the dealer primitive); `crates/engine/src/game/interaction.rs`; `crates/engine/src/ai_support/candidates.rs`; `crates/phase-ai/src/search.rs` (`deterministic_choice`, `fallback_action` only — `large_board_main_phase_has_no_development_sources` is Phase 11's edit in the same file); `client/src/types.ts`; the GamePage mulligan-button component (locate at phase start); `client/src/i18n/locales/en/game.json` (mirrors regenerate per the repo's i18n tooling, no manual per-locale edit).

**Claims to establish.**
- `handle_mulligan_decision`'s `MulliganChoice::Mulligan` arm redraws immediately on submission (`shuffle_hand_into_library` + `draw_n` called inline, no declare/interleave step) — confirmed at `mulligan.rs:219-241` at `BASE_SHA`. Re-confirm at phase start; this is the gap the declare round fills.
- With `grants_free_first_mulligan()` false and 2 seats, `free_first_mulligan()` is false, so `mulligan_count == 0` means "no regular mulligan yet" — this is a property of the *existing* mulligan-count logic the brief asserts holds for any 2-player format with that axis false; buy by reading `free_first_mulligan`'s definition at phase start (Dandan-specific: Phase 1 already set `grants_free_first_mulligan() → false` for Dandan).

**Verification plan.** Declare-round test: both seats declare (one Mulligan, one Keep) before either redraws, then redraws happen interleaved active-player-first (revert-failing: without the round, the eager-redraw path from the pre-existing `Mulligan` arm redraws immediately on that seat's own declaration). FreeReveal test: a qualifying hand (per settled decision 1) may FreeReveal once, before any regular mulligan, with a hostile fixture — a hand that qualifies only after a prior regular mulligan must be rejected (`mulligan_count > 0`). AI emission test: `deterministic_choice`/`fallback_action` emit FreeReveal when legal. Client/locale wiring is `DEFERRED` to no later phase — the `en` locale addition lands in this phase alongside the engine choice; UI-only cosmetic assertions are out of scope per the frontend-display convention (S7 is the pile-display phase; this phase's UI change is the mulligan-button label/handler, covered by an existing frontend test pattern if one exists for `UseSerumPowder`'s button, otherwise noted as a residual per Task-scope-and-verification-work).

**Deferral list.** In-game (post-mulligan) simultaneous draws — e.g. Day's Undoing's wheel — are Phase 9's job; this phase's dealer primitive is reused there, not reimplemented.

**Seam notes.** `crates/engine/src/game/mulligan.rs` builds on Phase 3's now-correct `shuffle_hand_into_library` routing. `crates/phase-ai/src/search.rs` shares the file with Phase 5 (mechanical swap, different lines) and Phase 11 (semantic fix, different lines).

**T1∧T2 check.** 1 unit (one interactive-choice addition + its declare-round machinery, per the anchor's own "routine interactive effect wiring types/parser/resolver/frontend/AI is one unit" example). T1 fails regardless of T2 — conjunction cannot fire.

