### Phase 9 — S4b + PREREQ-3 + S6: In-game simultaneous-draw dealer, Day's Undoing wheel split, deck-out verification

**Goal.** Build the general in-game simultaneous-draw dealer frame (every draw is a CR 121.2 instruction frame with CR 121.2a instruction-level and CR 121.6b per-unit replacement consults, and a pause can happen at any unit): a multi-player dealer frame settles each player's instruction count first, then deals single draws round-robin (active player first, via `apnap_order_from` with the ability's `starting_with`), surviving unit pauses and keeping each player's delivered count intact (`install_previous_effect_counts_by_player`). Intercept at the two fan-out layers in `effects/mod.rs::resolve_chain_body` (the `player_scope` driver and `resolves_for_each_target_player`), using the shape-gated-simultaneous-protocol precedent `scoped_library_search::supports_simultaneous_delivery` (confirmed present). Bump `RESOLUTION_STATE_WIRE_VERSION`. Apply this to Day's Undoing per settled decision 2: every hand and the shared graveyard are shuffled into the shared library once, then 14 cards are dealt one at a time, active player first, through the dealer — this needs the existing sequential per-player wheel (pinned by `tests/integration/all_player_library_wheel.rs`, confirmed present, kept together per the brief by `is_player_scope_local_continuation`) split into an all-players move/shuffle phase followed by a dealt-draw phase. Close S6 (deck-out) as verification only: the loss logic (`sba.rs::collect_draw_from_empty_losers` → `elimination::eliminate_players_simultaneously`) is unchanged; the flag path (`select_cards_to_draw` → `apply_draw_after_replacement` → `resolve_and_apply_cards_drawn` → `apply_resolved_ledger_edit`) was already routed in Phase 3 — this phase's own dealer must not park once any player has flagged empty (the pause hazard: `engine.rs::reconcile_terminal_result` runs SBAs when a player-loss SBA is pending during a resolution prompt, and a pause between two empty draws would turn a simultaneous draw into a single loser).

**Scope rule.** `crates/engine/src/game/effects/draw.rs`; `crates/engine/src/game/effects/mod.rs` (`resolve_chain_body`, standing shared-registration file); `crates/engine/src/types/resolution.rs` (`RESOLUTION_STATE_WIRE_VERSION` bump, `DrawSequenceStack` extension if needed); `crates/engine/src/game/effects/scoped_library_search.rs` (precedent trace; edit only if the wheel-split shares its dispatch); the file implementing the Day's Undoing all-player-wheel resolver (locate via `tests/integration/all_player_library_wheel.rs`'s target at phase start); `crates/engine/tests/integration/all_player_library_wheel.rs` (update the pinned test for the new wheel split, per the test's own discriminating-test contract — not a fixture, a product test); a new S6 test file under `crates/engine/tests/integration/`.

**Claims to establish.**
- `tests/integration/all_player_library_wheel.rs` exists and pins the sequential per-player wheel from #8757 (confirmed present at `BASE_SHA`) — re-read its assertions at phase start to know exactly what the wheel-split must preserve for non-Dandan formats (the split must be gated so other formats keep the existing sequential-wheel behavior unchanged).
- `scoped_library_search::supports_simultaneous_delivery` exists as the shape-gate precedent (confirmed at `BASE_SHA`) — its call site in `resolve_chain_body` is the intercept pattern to follow.

**Verification plan.** Day's Undoing fixture (settled decision 2, fully specified): both hands and the shared graveyard shuffle into the shared library once, then 14 cards deal one at a time active-player-first; sibling case — the same card in a non-shared-zone format keeps the pre-existing sequential per-player wheel unchanged (revert-failing on the gate: remove the shared-zone check, Dandan gets the old sequential wheel and the deal-order assertion fails). S6: pile-empty (CR 104.4a draw — both lose) and pile-short-by-one-under-the-dealer (the non-active player alone loses) as two hostile fixtures in one test file; the pause-hazard case (an empty draw with an intervening prompt) is asserted not to occur for the Dandan card list specifically (no Dandan card has a draw replacement) — this is a documented scope limit, not a general pause-safety proof, and is stated as such in the test's own scope, not asserted as a general property.

**Deferral list.** None — S4b, PREREQ-3, and S6 close together; no further shared-zone draw work remains after this phase.

**Seam notes.** `crates/engine/src/game/effects/draw.rs` builds on Phase 3's `select_cards_to_draw` routing. `crates/engine/src/game/effects/mod.rs` is the chartered.md standing shared-registration file, implied rather than needing explicit extension.

**T1∧T2 check.** Up to 2 units if S6 counts as its own mechanic (dealer frame + wheel split as one unit; verification-only S6 as a second, thinner unit) or 1 unit if S6 is read as the dealer's own acceptance evidence. Taking the conservative (higher) count of 2: estimated scope paths ≈ 7 (draw.rs, mod.rs, resolution.rs, scoped_library_search.rs trace, the wheel-resolver file, the pinned wheel test, the new S6 test). T1 may fire, T2 (7 < 13) does not — conjunction cannot fire either way.

