### Phase 10 — S7: Frontend shared-pile display

**Goal.** Expose which seat holds the shared pile from the engine in a `derived` view (or a shared-pile descriptor), so the client never infers it — display-only, per the project's engine-owns-logic rule. Render the shared library and graveyard once, in `playerPiles` (keep ExilePile per seat); `OpponentSeatPane` is unreachable here (`isSplitBoardActive` requires seatCount > 2). Update the fly-to anchors in `AnimationOverlay.tsx` (keyed by owner id today — must resolve through the same shared-pile identity), `hooks/useCastableZoneObjects.ts`, `viewmodel/gameStateView.ts::getPlayerZoneIds`, `LibraryPile.tsx::isMyLibrary`. `DebugLibraryViewer` reads `derived.debug_library_cards`, so the engine-side derivation must use `library_of` (Phase 3's accessor).

**Scope rule.** The engine-side derived-view file that computes `debug_library_cards` and any new shared-pile-holder field (locate at phase start — likely `crates/engine/src/game/derived.rs` or `derived_views.rs`, both already in the Phase 4/5 read-sweep scope for their own occurrences; this phase's edit is additive, a new field/method, not a further read-sweep edit); `client/src/pages/GamePage.tsx`; `client/src/components/AnimationOverlay.tsx`; `client/src/hooks/useCastableZoneObjects.ts`; `client/src/viewmodel/gameStateView.ts`; `client/src/components/LibraryPile.tsx`.

**Claims to establish.** None load-bearing beyond Phase 3's already-established accessor existing and being read-through by the derived view — no other code-state claim gates this phase's design.

**Verification plan.** A frontend test (existing pattern for pile rendering, e.g. `LibraryPile`/`GamePage` component tests) asserting: with a Dandan-shaped game state, the shared library/graveyard render once under `playerPiles` for both seats' views, not duplicated or split; `AnimationOverlay`'s fly-to anchor resolves to the shared-pile-holder's DOM node regardless of which seat is the local viewer (revert-failing: without the fix, the anchor keys by `owner id` and the non-canonical seat's animation targets a pile that doesn't visually exist for it).

**Deferral list.** None.

**Seam notes.** None with other engine-side phases beyond reading Phase 3's accessor.

**T1∧T2 check.** 1 unit (display-only exposure of one identity signal across its render sites). T1 fails regardless of T2 — conjunction cannot fire.

