### Phase 11 — S8: AI consumer rerouting

**Goal.** Route AI heuristics' raw library/graveyard reads through the engine accessor and fix the semantic double-counting/bias this introduces: `policies/payoff.rs::mill_scale` (opponent reading 0 today pins urgency HIGH — read through the accessor instead), `policies/mill_targeting.rs::verdict` (empty-library penalty always-on today), `threat_profile.rs::build_threat_profile_multiplayer` (returns `None` for the seat holding no pile — read through accessor), `zone_eval.rs::graveyard_value` (read through `graveyard_of` so both seats score the shared graveyard identically, canceling in `player_zone_score`'s me-minus-opponent difference instead of crediting it wholly to the canonical seat), `search.rs::large_board_main_phase_has_no_development_sources` (`player.graveyard.is_empty()` through `graveyard_of`). `deck_knowledge.rs::known_remaining_deck_counts`/`remaining_deck_view` look the deck pool up for the pile holder and, for shared-zone cards, drop the `object.owner != player` filter so every non-token card outside the shared library is subtracted regardless of owner. `policies/draw_payoff.rs` needs no change (already correct through `can_draw_at_least_one`). Close with a liveness test: `run_ai_actions_bounded` on a Dandan state (no `ai_duel` format flag exists, so an in-crate test is cheaper than a new mode).

**Scope rule.** `crates/phase-ai/src/policies/payoff.rs`; `crates/phase-ai/src/policies/mill_targeting.rs`; `crates/phase-ai/src/threat_profile.rs`; `crates/phase-ai/src/zone_eval.rs`; `crates/phase-ai/src/search.rs` (`large_board_main_phase_has_no_development_sources` only — distinct from Phase 8's edits to the same file); `crates/phase-ai/src/deck_knowledge.rs`.

**Claims to establish.**
- `zone_eval.rs::graveyard_value` today credits the shared graveyard's value wholly to the canonical seat in `player_zone_score`'s difference — this is a live bias the fix corrects, buy by reading the function's current read path at phase start (it will read the raw `player.graveyard` field, not an accessor, since Phase 5's mechanical swap on this file only swaps the *reference*, not the *semantics* — confirm Phase 5 landed the mechanical swap first).
- `ai_duel` has no general-format flag, only Commander modes — buy by grepping `ai_duel`'s CLI flag definitions at phase start; this is why the liveness check is an in-crate test, not a new `ai_duel` mode.

**Verification plan.** For each rerouted heuristic, a unit test comparing the Dandan-config score against the pre-fix (raw-read) score on an identical shared-graveyard/library state, showing the bias is gone (revert-failing: revert the accessor swap on that one function, the biased score returns). Liveness test: `run_ai_actions_bounded` completes without panicking on a Dandan state through several turns (a positive reach-guard: assert at least one legal action was taken by each seat, not just "didn't crash").

**Deferral list.** None — this phase closes the run's AI-facing work.

**Seam notes.** `crates/phase-ai/src/search.rs` and `crates/phase-ai/src/zone_eval.rs`/`policies/payoff.rs`/`policies/mill_targeting.rs` share files with Phase 5's mechanical read-swap (different lines/purpose, sequential — this phase's semantic fix depends on Phase 5's accessor swap already being in place).

**T1∧T2 check.** 1 unit (one "route AI reads through the shared-zone accessor and correct the resulting bias" mechanic, six lockstep call sites). T1 fails regardless of T2 — conjunction cannot fire.

